us.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.record-257rig-c16"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.record-257rig-c16"],"id":"long.record-257rig-c16","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.84 (A square-root carry bound implies half-membership)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.84, p. 68, label record:257rig-c16","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Write $G$ for the greedy support and $C_G(N)$ for its centred carry. If\n$$\n\\forall N,\\qquad C_G(N) \\le 2\\sqrt N + 4,\n$$\nthen the greedy selected support $G$ is infinite and $X_G(2)=1/2$. Nonnegativity of $C_G$ is unconditional (see Theorem 6.11 and the greedy case above); only the upper $2\\sqrt N+4$ bound remains open. This is a different hypothesis from the dyadic-band condition and the largest-skip condition; logical independence is not asserted.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.record-257rig-c16","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.record-257rig-c16","id":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.record-257rig-c16%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.HalfCarryReachability.greedy_half_infinite_of_mobiusCenteredHalfCarry_upperBound%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.record-257rig-c16%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.HalfCarryReachability.greedy_half_infinite_of_mobiusCenteredHalfCarry_upperBound%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/lean.Erdos249257.HalfCarryReachability.greedy_half_infinite_of_mobiusCenteredHalfCarry_upperBound"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.record-257rig